<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CycloneDDS tuning for a multi-robot graph.

  WHAT THIS FIXES

    Every ROS 2 node is a DDS participant, and CycloneDDS assigns each one an
    index within the domain. The default MaxAutoParticipantIndex is 9, so the
    tenth participant onwards has to find a free slot and, past the limit, simply
    cannot:

      [controller_server] Failed to find a free participant index for domain 0
      [rmw_cyclonedds_cpp] rmw_create_node: failed to create domain, error Error
      terminate called after throwing an instance of 'rclcpp::exceptions::RCLError'
        what():  failed to initialize rcl node

    One robot fits under the default. Two do not: two Nav2 stacks are 14 nodes on
    their own, and with two slam_toolbox, two SensorBSP, two SafetyGates, the
    plant nodes and static transform publishers per robot, plus the fleet map and
    the costmap filter servers, the graph is around forty participants.

    The failure is loud but misleading. It is thrown by whichever nodes happen to
    start last, so it reads as "the second robot's Nav2 is broken" rather than
    "the host ran out of participant indices" - and the first robot comes up
    perfectly, which makes it look like a namespacing bug.

  WHY 120

    Room for roughly ten robots' worth of stack, matching the assignment's
    "scale to 10+ robots" requirement, so that scaling the fleet stays an edit to
    fleet.yaml rather than a second environment problem to rediscover.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <Discovery>
      <MaxAutoParticipantIndex>120</MaxAutoParticipantIndex>
    </Discovery>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
